1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:05,944
Host: Welcome to KC desk note. Today we are unpacking one fresh research report and the question it raises.

2
00:00:06,304 --> 00:00:11,134
Host: Welcome back to our podcast. Today we’re looking at a fresh report on the offshore renminbi.

3
00:00:11,494 --> 00:00:19,157
Guest: That’s right. The report argues that CNH is set to outperform, driven by strong capital flows and a supportive policy-related backdrop.

4
00:00:19,517 --> 00:00:22,257
Host: So what’s the core question this report is trying to answer?

5
00:00:22,617 --> 00:00:30,279
Guest: It’s really about whether the renminbi can continue to strengthen even when the US dollar is strong. The answer, based on the data, is yes.

6
00:00:30,639 --> 00:00:34,540
Host: Let’s dig into the first key insight. What’s driving this outperformance?

7
00:00:34,900 --> 00:00:43,352
Guest: The first big factor is China’s strong external sector. Despite the US dollar index rising, USD/CNH has actually fallen. That’s unusual.

8
00:00:43,712 --> 00:00:46,684
Host: So the renminbi is behaving differently than other currencies?

9
00:00:47,044 --> 00:00:55,914
Guest: Exactly. The sensitivity of USD/CNH to a rising dollar is only about 28%, but when the dollar falls, that sensitivity jumps to 62%.

10
00:00:56,274 --> 00:00:57,946
Guest: So there’s an asymmetric response.

11
00:00:58,306 --> 00:01:03,415
Host: That suggests the market is already pricing in a stronger renminbi. What’s the second insight?

12
00:01:03,775 --> 00:01:12,552
Guest: Corporate FX repatriation is a major driver. In April, net FX trade settlement hit over 47 billion dollars. Exporters are bringing money back onshore.

13
00:01:12,912 --> 00:01:14,259
Host: Why are they doing that now?

14
00:01:14,619 --> 00:01:18,473
Guest: Strong export growth and expectations for further renminbi appreciation.

15
00:01:18,833 --> 00:01:24,174
Guest: The report notes that a de-escalation in the Middle East could be a catalyst for even more repatriation.

16
00:01:24,534 --> 00:01:28,388
Host: So the flow dynamics are very supportive. What about the policy-related side?

17
00:01:28,748 --> 00:01:35,714
Guest: The recent Xi-Trump summit has created a constructive backdrop. Foreign inflows into China-focused equity ETFs jumped after the meeting,

18
00:01:36,074 --> 00:01:38,489
Guest: totaling over 2 billion dollars month-to-date.

19
00:01:38,849 --> 00:01:42,982
Host: That’s a clear signal of improved sentiment. Are there any technical factors at play?

20
00:01:43,342 --> 00:01:49,983
Guest: Yes. The daily USD/CNY fixing has been drifting lower, even with a stronger dollar. That’s a deliberate signal from the authorities.

21
00:01:50,343 --> 00:01:53,037
Host: And what about valuation? Is the renminbi cheap?

22
00:01:53,397 --> 00:02:00,409
Guest: According to the report, the renminbi is undervalued by an average of 9.5% across four models. That’s a significant discount.

23
00:02:00,769 --> 00:02:06,435
Host: So the case for a stronger renminbi seems pretty solid. But what doesn’t the report fully settle?

24
00:02:06,795 --> 00:02:14,132
Guest: One open question is the impact of any renewed US dollar strength. The report acknowledges that a stronger dollar could temporarily slow the downtrend.

25
00:02:14,492 --> 00:02:18,718
Host: So there’s still some uncertainty there. That’s a good reason to read the full report.

26
00:02:19,078 --> 00:02:24,605
Guest: Absolutely. The report also has detailed charts on FX settlement and exporter behavior that are worth exploring.

27
00:02:24,965 --> 00:02:30,305
Host: Thanks for breaking that down. For our listeners, we’ll leave the link to the full report in the show notes.

28
00:02:30,665 --> 00:02:36,099
Guest: And if you want to discuss the trade ideas or the valuation models, join the conversation in our community.

29
00:02:36,459 --> 00:02:39,152
Host: Thanks for listening, and we’ll see you next time.
